["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"epistemic-knowledge-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0dc9e-2796-77ca-8d20-46fb5adbf156","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"epic","fields":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 22–29, § 44–46, § 52–53. Interpretation is separated from integration; what cannot be\nrepresented canonically is parked, not discarded and not forced. Entity resolution is the\nhighest-risk semantic operation and is therefore an explicit transaction.\n\n## Outcome\n\nCrates `ekr-incubate`, `ekr-interpret`, `ekr-integrate`:\n\n- transient roots with their own stable schemas (§ 22, § 53), `RootUtility` metadata (§ 40);\n- the interpretation session contract (amendment 85, A5): immutable request bytes with digests, one\n  disposition per signal including no-ops with a `basis`, receipts, a bounded number of visits;\n- the resolver (A10): typed references, explicit merge and split transactions with lineage\n  (§ 45–46), no string matching;\n- integration plans with versioned, conditional mappings (§ 27–28, § 52); contradiction produces\n  `Disputed` (§ 44), never a silent loser.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nThe § 63 Slack-to-canonical fixture commits the proposal and, on the confirming message, the fact;\na parked root integrates after a mapping is added; a wrong merge is reverted by a split with\nprovenance intact.\n\n## Carries\n\nA5, A10.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-90337225a8e40a49927831105a0392b2","locator":"ep://planning/store/epic/p3-incubation-integration","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":1,"type":"aep.epic/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 22–29, § 44–46, § 52–53. Interpretation is separated from integration; what cannot be\nrepresented canonically is parked, not discarded and not forced. Entity resolution is the\nhighest-risk semantic operation and is therefore an explicit transaction.\n\n## Outcome\n\nCrates `ekr-incubate`, `ekr-interpret`, `ekr-integrate`:\n\n- transient roots with their own stable schemas (§ 22, § 53), `RootUtility` metadata (§ 40);\n- the interpretation session contract (amendment 85, A5): immutable request bytes with digests, one\n  disposition per signal including no-ops with a `basis`, receipts, a bounded number of visits;\n- the resolver (A10): typed references, explicit merge and split transactions with lineage\n  (§ 45–46), no string matching;\n- integration plans with versioned, conditional mappings (§ 27–28, § 52); contradiction produces\n  `Disputed` (§ 44), never a silent loser.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nThe § 63 Slack-to-canonical fixture commits the proposal and, on the confirming message, the fact;\na parked root integrates after a mapping is added; a wrong merge is reverted by a split with\nprovenance intact.\n\n## Carries\n\nA5, A10.\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"initiative:epistemic-knowledge-runtime"},{"depends_on":"epic:p2-observation-layer"},{"serves":"vision:o5"}],"status":"draft","title":"P3 — Incubation, interpretation, integration"},"lifecycle_state":"draft"},"relations":[{"decomposes":"initiative:epistemic-knowledge-runtime"},{"depends_on":"epic:p2-observation-layer"},{"serves":"vision:o5"}],"title":"P3 — Incubation, interpretation, integration"},"id":"ent-90337225a8e40a49927831105a0392b2","lifecycle_state":"draft","revision":1,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["epic","ent-90337225a8e40a49927831105a0392b2"]}]